{"title":"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Table)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Table)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_Using_Infinite_Geometric_Series\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution Using Infinite Geometric Series</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three balls are randomly and independently tossed into bins numbered with the positive integers so that for each ball, the probability that it is tossed into bin <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65baa1cd247bf018d2dc0ed082fa82a3bf50b343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{-i}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/9/a896979d2354a21dd1dc842062e75f7cb0b602f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1,2,3,....$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"17\" /> More than one ball is allowed in each bin. The probability that the balls end up evenly spaced in distinct bins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/2/4f28853fb56a9e11580d445ffe40c2c239f0be66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac pq,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"17\" height=\"36\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. (For example, the balls are evenly spaced if they are tossed into bins <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/d/c6dd7470632000b66b0544b7a456b09a11341865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,17,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b833a70e5b34465a7e1cc445231d569f21b81da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />) What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22dd6d9587b2fe28d6b8fd7d058a3e8326763199.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/f/47f5714954b1b9acbd418fb8ae6c99a6da038b8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }55 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }56 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }57\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }58 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }59$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>\"Evenly spaced\" just means the bins form an arithmetic sequence.\n</p><p>Suppose the middle bin in the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4baf6d4b1cfa69b68b3204b5e2eba0c5755fe20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> different possibilities for the first bin, and these two bins uniquely determine the final bin. Now, the probability that these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> bins are chosen is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/6709054b4e896d7c95f3d9a0c5163277dca8a378.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\cdot 2^{-3x} = 6\\cdot \\frac{1}{8^x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"122\" height=\"37\" />, so the probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the middle bin is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b53c998a5c40235f55044ac6075c16841307226.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\cdot\\frac{x-1}{8^x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"66\" height=\"37\" />. Then, we want the sum\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4e8a5fe7a2883542996d2dcfb9c853821ba4491.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 6\\sum_{x=2}^{\\infty}\\frac{x-1}{8^x} &amp;= \\frac{6}{8}\\left[\\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{2}{8^2} + \\frac{3}{8^3}\\cdots\\right]\\\\ &amp;= \\frac34\\left[\\left(\\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{8^2} + \\frac{1}{8^3}+\\cdots \\right) + \\left(\\frac{1}{8^2} + \\frac{1}{8^3} + \\frac{1}{8^4} + \\cdots \\right) + \\cdots\\right]\\\\ &amp;= \\frac34\\left[\\frac17\\cdot \\left(1 + \\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{8^2} + \\frac{1}{8^3} + \\cdots \\right)\\right]\\\\ &amp;= \\frac34\\cdot \\frac{8}{49}\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{6}{49} \\end{align*}\" width=\"559\" height=\"234\" />\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906b05b5219d98a0f982a40499beea6cb28a1b24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+49=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }55}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"142\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in solution 1, note that \"evenly spaced\" means the bins are in arithmetic sequence. We let the first bin be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and the common difference be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Further note that each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/7/347230b1823d4a8f8b932dc6667582c654e800da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> pair uniquely determines a set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> bins. \n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06d5dd57a404f3493262280c2b27fce443b1550c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" /> because the leftmost bin in the sequence can be any bin, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/385694583d5b99d2ad7b9180f00a1503aefc698a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d\\geq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, because the bins must be distinct.\n</p><p>This gives us the following sum for the probability:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57cd55b3a81dd8db425ebea2b046defc8d3c4211.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 6 \\sum_{a=1}^{\\infty} \\sum_{d=1}^{\\infty} 2^{-3a-3d} &amp;= 6 \\sum_{a=1}^{\\infty} \\sum_{d=1}^{\\infty} 2^{-3a} \\cdot 2^{-3d} \\\\ &amp;= 6 \\left( \\sum_{a=1}^{\\infty} 2^{-3a} \\right) \\left( \\sum_{d=1}^{\\infty} 2^{-3d} \\right) \\\\ &amp;= 6 \\left( \\sum_{a=1}^{\\infty} 8^{-a} \\right) \\left( \\sum_{d=1}^{\\infty} 8^{-d} \\right) \\\\ &amp;= 6 \\left( \\frac{1}{7} \\right) \\left( \\frac{1}{7} \\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{6}{49} .\\end{align*}\" width=\"344\" height=\"263\" />\nTherefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0b9bef3f4b1e0eeed09a4fde695923377a61c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 49 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }55}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"141\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-Darren Yao\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This is a slightly messier variant of solution 2. If the first ball is in bin <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> and the second ball is in bin <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/248ee41acf29d8dac6d244350970db2cb67e3e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j&gt;i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" />, then the third ball is in bin <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a29d66807625f6c6d2f8a0d1b03d56c80ac91ebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2j-i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" />. Thus the probability is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6bbb8f1a7137427644bacd793cdfa55dd8d7412.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 6\\sum_{i=1}^{\\infty}\\sum_{j=i+1}^\\infty2^{-i}2^{-j}2^{-2j+i}&amp;=6\\sum_{i=1}^{\\infty}\\sum_{j=i+1}^\\infty2^{-3j}\\\\ &amp;=6\\sum_{i=1}^{\\infty}\\left(\\frac{2^{-3(i+1)}}{1-\\tfrac{1}{8}}\\right)\\\\ &amp;=6\\sum_{i=1}^\\infty\\frac{8}{7}\\cdot2^{-3}\\cdot2^{-3i}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{6}{7}\\sum_{i=1}^\\infty2^{-3i}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{6}{7}\\cdot\\frac{2^{-3}}{1-\\tfrac18}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{6}{49}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"342\" height=\"320\" />\nTherefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0b9bef3f4b1e0eeed09a4fde695923377a61c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 49 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }55}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"141\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Table.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Table)\">Solution 4 (Table)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Table)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Based on the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54e7152acd659788861f0453ac195c635e0a005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> we construct the following table:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a841f23b85855ed24ba8668ea9779ff90c455eb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}  &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex] \\textbf{Exactly }\\boldsymbol{n}\\textbf{ Spaces Apart} &amp; \\textbf{Bin \\#s} &amp; \\textbf{Expression} &amp; \\textbf{Prob. of One Such Perm.} \\\\ [1ex]  \\hline\\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex]  n=1 &amp; 1,2,3 &amp; 2^{-1}\\cdot2^{-2}\\cdot2^{-3} &amp; 2^{-6} \\\\ [1ex]   &amp; 2,3,4 &amp; 2^{-2}\\cdot2^{-3}\\cdot2^{-4} &amp; 2^{-9} \\\\ [1ex]   &amp; 3,4,5 &amp; 2^{-3}\\cdot2^{-4}\\cdot2^{-5} &amp; 2^{-12} \\\\ [1ex]   &amp; 4,5,6 &amp; 2^{-4}\\cdot2^{-5}\\cdot2^{-6} &amp; 2^{-15} \\\\ [1ex]   &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\cdots \\\\ [1ex]  \\hline  &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex]  n=2 &amp; 1,3,5 &amp; 2^{-1}\\cdot2^{-3}\\cdot2^{-5} &amp; 2^{-9} \\\\ [1ex]   &amp; 2,4,6 &amp; 2^{-2}\\cdot2^{-4}\\cdot2^{-6} &amp; 2^{-12} \\\\ [1ex]   &amp; 3,5,7 &amp; 2^{-3}\\cdot2^{-5}\\cdot2^{-7} &amp; 2^{-15} \\\\ [1ex]   &amp; 4,6,8 &amp; 2^{-4}\\cdot2^{-6}\\cdot2^{-8} &amp; 2^{-18} \\\\ [1ex]   &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\cdots \\\\ [1ex]  \\hline  &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex]  n=3 &amp; 1,4,7 &amp; 2^{-1}\\cdot2^{-4}\\cdot2^{-7} &amp; 2^{-12} \\\\ [1ex]   &amp; 2,5,8 &amp; 2^{-2}\\cdot2^{-5}\\cdot2^{-8} &amp; 2^{-15} \\\\ [1ex]   &amp; 3,6,9 &amp; 2^{-3}\\cdot2^{-6}\\cdot2^{-9} &amp; 2^{-18} \\\\ [1ex]  &amp; 4,7,10 &amp; 2^{-4}\\cdot2^{-7}\\cdot2^{-10} &amp; 2^{-21} \\\\ [1ex]  &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\cdots \\\\ [1ex]  \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex]    \\cdots &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\cdots \\\\ [1ex] \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"653\" height=\"514\" />\nSince three balls have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3920c5e3f6b2e5749cd75c3853b63ae714d00561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> permutations, the requested probability is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/a/eca4db8fb88a8f237f66b28d1a316ff4c9cf11dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 6\\left(\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}2^{-6-3k}+\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}2^{-9-3k}+\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}2^{-12-3k}+\\cdots\\right)&amp;=6\\left(2^{-6}\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}2^{-3k}+2^{-9}\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}2^{-3k}+2^{-12}\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}2^{-3k}+\\cdots\\right) \\\\ &amp;=\\left(6\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}2^{-3k}\\right)\\cdot\\left(2^{-6}+2^{-9}+2^{-12}+\\cdots\\right) \\\\ &amp;=\\left(6\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}2^{-3k}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}2^{-6-3k}\\right) \\\\ &amp;=\\left(6\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}2^{-3k}\\right)\\cdot\\left(2^{-6}\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}2^{-3k}\\right) \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{6}{1-2^{-3}}\\cdot\\frac{2^{-6}}{1-2^{-3}} \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{6}{49} \\end{align*}\" width=\"813\" height=\"325\" />\nby infinite geometric series, from which the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906b05b5219d98a0f982a40499beea6cb28a1b24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+49=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }55}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"142\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/x16YUmd0OqY\">https://youtu.be/x16YUmd0OqY</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_IvLCWSSDFs\">https://youtu.be/_IvLCWSSDFs</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_Using_Infinite_Geometric_Series\">Video Solution Using Infinite Geometric Series</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution Using Infinite Geometric Series\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3B-3_nOTIu4\">https://youtu.be/3B-3_nOTIu4</a>\n</p><p>~hippopotamus1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsect